# CoW true-lazy P3 tier-1 — index-read bind + user-method-mutate witness.
#
# `Vector[int] x = coll[0]` binds an element via index read. `x.bump(99)`
# calls a USER method `bump(&self, ...)` that pushes onto its receiver —
# a `&self` (mutable-borrow) self-convention. The TYPED user-method path
# (fn_borrow_params[key][0]) classifies `bump` as mutating its receiver,
# so the scan marks `x` mutated and the bind does NOT flip — `x` is an
# eager-cloned independent owner. The eager-clone observed value (the
# pre-mutation snapshot for coll[0]; x carries its own pushed copy) is the
# SOUND tier-1 outcome (tier-2's liveness gate recovers the borrow). No
# UAF / double-free: x and coll[0] are independent.
equip [T] Vector[T]:
    void bump(&self, T v):
        self.push(v)

void main():
    Vector[Vector[int]] coll = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
    Vector[int] x = coll[0]
    x.bump(99)
    print(coll[0].len())
    print(x.len())
